{"nodes": [{"id": "extracted_archives_restore_point_2_13_lambda_spectra_bound_figure", "label": "The bound on \u039b_spectra \u2014 118 or 120", "file_type": "document", "source_file": "extracted/archives/restore-point-2-13/lambda-spectra-bound.html", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "An interactive (Z, charge) plot built to settle whether extending the atomic bound from Z=118 to Z=120 changes the closure of \u039b_spectra. It answers by showing the two runs side by side rather than by argument."}, {"id": "extracted_archives_restore_point_2_13_lambda_spectra_bound_lambda_spectra", "label": "\u039b_spectra (the (Z, charge) face)", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "extracted/archives/restore-point-2-13/lambda-spectra-bound.html", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Every cell of the index is one ion, addressed by (Z, charge); the face is the coordinate pair the bound question lives on."}, {"id": "extracted_archives_restore_point_2_13_lambda_spectra_bound_bound_z_118", "label": "Bound Z = 118", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "extracted/archives/restore-point-2-13/lambda-spectra-bound.html", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "The bound taken from the elements that actually exist: 7,021 (Z, charge) pairs, 101,328 cells, 901,200 refused by rule."}, {"id": "extracted_archives_restore_point_2_13_lambda_spectra_bound_bound_z_120", "label": "Bound Z = 120", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "extracted/archives/restore-point-2-13/lambda-spectra-bound.html", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "The extended bound: +239 pairs, +3,504 cells, +30,768 refused. It adds the pale wedge at Z=119 and Z=120."}, {"id": "extracted_archives_restore_point_2_13_lambda_spectra_bound_closure_e_zero", "label": "E(\u039b_spectra) = 0 under either bound", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "extracted/archives/restore-point-2-13/lambda-spectra-bound.html", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Closure is indifferent to the choice of bound because both generating rules are total and return a fibre for every N; E = 0 is structural, not a discovery about the elements."}, {"id": "extracted_archives_restore_point_2_13_lambda_spectra_bound_charge_le_z_rule", "label": "Triangle rule: charge \u2264 Z", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "extracted/archives/restore-point-2-13/lambda-spectra-bound.html", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "The admissibility rule that makes the face a triangle; 901,200 of the grid's cells are refused by it at Z=118, and a refusal carries a reason."}, {"id": "extracted_archives_restore_point_2_13_lambda_spectra_bound_isoelectronic_count", "label": "Isoelectronic count N = Z \u2212 charge + 1", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "extracted/archives/restore-point-2-13/lambda-spectra-bound.html", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "The up-right diagonals of the face; each diagonal is one electron count, which is what the multiplicity fibre is indexed by."}, {"id": "extracted_archives_restore_point_2_13_lambda_spectra_bound_multiplicity_fibre", "label": "Multiplicity fibre", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "extracted/archives/restore-point-2-13/lambda-spectra-bound.html", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "The set of values the generating rule returns for an electron count N. A fibre of size 1 marks an aufbau opening; size 2 is the doubled case."}, {"id": "extracted_archives_restore_point_2_13_lambda_spectra_bound_aufbau_opening", "label": "Aufbau opening (fibre = 1)", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "extracted/archives/restore-point-2-13/lambda-spectra-bound.html", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Electron counts where one electron begins a new subshell \u2014 1s at N=1 through 8s at N=119. The singleton fibre is the signature."}, {"id": "extracted_archives_restore_point_2_13_lambda_spectra_bound_witnessed_cells_358", "label": "358 witnessed cells (unchanged by the bound)", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "extracted/archives/restore-point-2-13/lambda-spectra-bound.html", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "The row that actually moves the argument: witnessed cells and 'cells an instrument could ever fill' are identical at both bounds."}, {"id": "extracted_archives_restore_point_2_13_lambda_spectra_bound_no_atom_exists_at_119_120", "label": "Added cells are not witnessable", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "extracted/archives/restore-point-2-13/lambda-spectra-bound.html", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "The 3,504 cells at Z=119 and Z=120 are neither refused (refusal carries a reason) nor unwitnessed-with-a-bound (there is no bound to name) \u2014 no atom exists to be witnessed."}], "edges": [{"source": "extracted_archives_restore_point_2_13_lambda_spectra_bound_figure", "target": "extracted_archives_restore_point_2_13_lambda_spectra_bound_lambda_spectra", "relation": "references", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "extracted/archives/restore-point-2-13/lambda-spectra-bound.html", "source_location": null, "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "extracted_archives_restore_point_2_13_lambda_spectra_bound_figure", "target": "extracted_archives